    "custom_multicolumns_xpBCAp": {
      "type": "custom-multicolumns",
      "blocks": {
        "column_W4R47Y": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "link": "",
            "dynamic_costs": "",
            "custom_text_hover": "",
            "title": "",
            "show_text_double_column": false,
            "text": "<p>The Tysoe Street shop is such a quirky building, tall and triangular, it was not at first glance the perfect shape for a kitchen showroom, but we loved the challenge and think that we have created a really interesting display which we hope encapsulates all that deVOL has to offer. We have a selection of Shaker, Heirloom and Sebastian Cox furniture on show, painted in our standard colours and fitted with the loveliest worktops – prime oak, Carrara marble and bespoke aged copper</p>",
            "show_above_image": true,
            "link_label": "",
            "linked_product": ""
          }
        },
        "column_fB3ekK": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "link": "",
            "dynamic_costs": "",
            "custom_text_hover": "",
            "title": "",
            "show_text_double_column": false,
            "text": "<p>Intermingled amongst the cupboards is an impressive selection of deVOL accessories and freestanding pieces of furniture to admire. Walls adorned top to toe in our handmade tiles, lights from our Heirloom Collection, an iron pot hanger above the Lacanche cooker and café curtain rails with wispy white linen. There are aged brass taps and handcrafted knobs and our much-loved Helen's Stool sitting beautifully beneath our Dairy Table. There really is so much to see in just a couple of rooms.</p>",
            "show_above_image": true,
            "link_label": "",
            "linked_product": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "column_W4R47Y",
        "column_fB3ekK"
